You are working on a full-stack AI Analytics / BI platform.

The system consists of:
- React frontend (Vite + TypeScript)
- .NET 8 Web API backend
- AI integration layer using OpenAI (initially), later Azure OpenAI
- SQL Server database for analytics data

---

# ARCHITECTURE PRINCIPLES

1. Separation of concerns is strict:
   - React only handles UI and API calls
   - .NET API handles orchestration and business logic
   - AI services are isolated behind interfaces
   - Database logic is never exposed to frontend

2. AI is treated as a service, not business logic:
   - AI is used for SQL generation, summarization, and insights
   - AI outputs must be validated before execution
   - Deterministic code controls workflows and safety

3. Use clean architecture in backend:
   - API layer (controllers)
   - Application layer (services/workflows)
   - Domain layer (core models)
   - Infrastructure layer (DB, AI, external services)

---

# AI DESIGN RULES

- Always abstract OpenAI behind an interface (IAIProvider)
- Never call OpenAI directly from controllers
- Prompts must be centralized and reusable
- AI responses should be structured where possible (not free text only)
- SQL generation must be validated before execution
- Never allow AI-generated queries to execute destructive commands (DELETE, DROP, UPDATE)

---

# FRONTEND RULES

- React uses functional components and hooks
- API calls are centralized in a /api folder
- UI is minimal and functional (not over-engineered)
- Results from backend are rendered dynamically (schema-agnostic tables)
- No business logic in UI

---

# BACKEND RULES

- Controllers are thin (no business logic)
- Services handle all orchestration
- AI calls are made through IAIProvider abstraction
- SQL execution is isolated and safe
- Logging is included for AI prompts and outputs

---

# DEVELOPMENT PRIORITIES

1. Build vertical slices first:
   - Question → AI → SQL → DB → UI

2. Avoid premature optimization:
   - No microservices
   - No event-driven architecture (until needed)
   - No complex caching early

3. Focus on system behavior over structure perfection

---

# PROJECT GOAL

This project is a production-style AI analytics platform that demonstrates:
- LLM integration in real workflows
- SQL generation from natural language
- safe execution of AI-generated outputs
- clean architecture and system design
- observability and evaluation patterns

The goal is not a demo — it is a realistic enterprise-style AI system.